# state/* (not a plain "state/"), PRD-build-burst-gate-canary-invariant
# R15: git cannot re-include a file whose PARENT DIRECTORY is itself
# excluded ("state/" excludes the directory; "!state/cargo-producers.txt"
# below would then be silently powerless — confirmed via `git check-ignore
# -v` while landing R15). "state/*" excludes every top-level entry
# individually instead, which is functionally identical for everything
# else under state/ (each entry, file or directory, is still excluded,
# and an excluded directory's own contents still never get traversed) but
# leaves room for the one negation below.
state/*
# Explicit even though state/* already covers it (PRD-build-tenant-secret-
# continuity): runtime secrets a branch dispatch mints (tenant keys,
# tokens) must never be git-tracked, so this line stays true even if the
# blanket state/* entry above is ever narrowed.
state/secrets/
# PRD-build-burst-gate-canary-invariant R15: the ONE exception to the
# blanket state/* ignore above. Every other path under state/ is
# runtime-derived (sessions, ledgers, manifests) and must never be
# git-tracked; cargo-producers.txt is the opposite shape — an
# operator-authored policy list (which producers' cargo calls a
# burst-intended gate requires a ledger row for) that extend-gate.sh reads
# at gate time, no different in kind from a config file that happens to
# live under state/ by convention. Un-ignored so a fresh clone / a fresh
# box has the real list on disk, not an empty gate-blocking void.
!state/cargo-producers.txt
# PRD-build-land-conflict-resolver R2: same exception shape as
# cargo-producers.txt above — the negation must target state/land-policy
# itself (the top-level entry state/* excludes), not state/land-policy/*,
# per the R15 comment above (a file's parent directory being excluded
# can't be undone by negating the file alone). state/land-policy/<repo>.json
# is an operator-authored generated/append-only file list per target
# repo, not runtime-derived state.
!state/land-policy
*.lock
*.bak.*
repos/
target/
*.err
*.out
